## Item 1: storytime-cat — the path decision

Path A is not possible for the ordered look. The wolf kind has no open-mouth rest option: its
options are the wide `smile` grin or the tiny `smileArc` line, and the cat kind uses the line. It
does have a jaw bone and two clips that open it (`howl`, `attack`), but neither is an opt-in clip
that holds the mouth open, no clip named `sing` exists, and one clip cannot run with `sit`, so the
cat could not both sit on the fence and sing. The order also says "do not add a clip". Path A had
no form left.

Path B is taken: `openMouth?: boolean` on `assets/parts/cat-kind.ts`, default off, plus
`openMouth: true` in `assets/storytime-cat.ts`.

## Item 1: the build, one call (render --fast and inspect --fast)

First attempt: the `mouth-open` body was not visible from any view (buried inside the cream
muzzle, which is grown 4 mm over the head). Fix 1 of 2: the surface shell now grows 6 mm (2 mm
above the cream) and cuts 4 mm in. Re-render: `mouth-open` visible at 0.6 % of the front
silhouette and 0.3 % of the three-quarter. 0 further fixes.

Second attempt: 41,080 triangles with vertex colours, size 0.344 x 0.557 x 0.544 m, lowest point
y = -0.003 m, no `warning:` line. The inspect warnings name only the two mouth bodies of the kind
(`mouth`, `tongue`), which are inside the head at rest and show when the jaw opens; the source cat
holds the same two.

Looked at the render once: grey coat, darker grey tabby bands, white muzzle, chest, and paws,
amber eyes with lashes, pink nose and ear insides, dark whiskers, and a small dark open mouth with
a pink tongue under the nose. No cyan or teal patch anywhere.

